---
import { PRODUCT_NAME } from '../../config';

/** The signature's name. Not public yet, so the note is signed by role until it's set. */
const FOUNDER_NAME: string | null = null;
---
<section class="s wrap rule founder" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
  <div class="founder-in">
    <h2 id="why-h">Why I built {PRODUCT_NAME}</h2>
    <p>My agents were writing the code, opening the PRs, and sometimes merging them too. I couldn't keep up. I lost track of what was actually in my own repo, and the easy way out was to stop reading and just trust them.</p>
    <p>I didn't want that. I wanted the agents working for me, with me still in charge of what ships. So I built a Git client for that job.</p>
    <p>Now I open {PRODUCT_NAME} and I know what happened, where I'm needed, and what's still being worked on. When I need to do something by hand, it's still a full Git client underneath.</p>
    <p class="sig">— {FOUNDER_NAME ? `${FOUNDER_NAME}, who makes ${PRODUCT_NAME}` : `The person who makes ${PRODUCT_NAME}`}</p>
  </div>
</section>
